# A Json value on a Json kwarg arrives as the value ([NCBK.6.10]). The keys
# are written out of order, with a Float and an array besides. The call line
# renders a Json argument as its canonical text, unquoted, so a Json argument
# handed over as a string shows as a quoted one.
#
# `json:` marks a Json slot's value as a document rather than a String; the
# text may hold no spaces, since a scenario line splits on them.
assert Inbox k=1 response=json:{"ref":{"size":45002,"mime":"image/jpeg","backend":"fs","hash":"abab"},"tags":["a","b"],"ratio":0.5,"expires_at":1790000000}
pump
